# Notebook timing

Never define custom timing helpers (`time_ms`, `timeit.repeat` wrappers, etc.) in course notebooks.

Use Jupyter's **`%timeit`** magic instead, matching existing episodes (ep01, ep02):

```python
jax.block_until_ready(fn(x))  # warm up jit cache when needed

print("eager:")
%timeit jax.block_until_ready(fn(x))

print("jit:")
%timeit jax.block_until_ready(fn_jit(x))
```

For pure-Python loops (no async JAX dispatch), `%timeit fn(x)` is fine.

Do not add `import timeit` solely for benchmarking.
